{"event_id":"EVT-000081","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-30T17:07:42.864Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260830T130455733132Z","run_id":"RUN-TRF-009-20260830T170440522310Z","requirement_id":"TRF-009","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":4,"prior_feedback_history":["Repair the applicability logic: a missing or invalid constructionStageDate must not make the conditional requirement pass. Require a valid constructionStageDate and evaluate the deadline/method obligations only when that date is before 2003-09-01; otherwise report the missing applicability evidence rather than treating absence as non-applicability. Preserve the ship target, xsd:date operands, delivery-year-plus-20 deadline, and the two permitted method alternatives.","Preserve the required ship target, valid xsd:date constructionStageDate applicability evidence, IA/IA Super alternatives, and the two permitted compliance-method alternatives. Repair the conditional SPARQL violation logic: the expression `YEAR(?deliveryDate) + 20 < YEAR(?deliveryDate) + 20` is tautologically false and causes an accidental pass, and the current query incorrectly tests whether deliveryDate itself is 1 January rather than evaluating the twenty-year deadline. Include the supplied ship-owned assessmentDate for the deadline evaluation and compare it against 1 January of delivery year plus 20 using direct year/month/day logic without dynamic xsd:date construction; missing deliveryDate or method must remain a violation only for applicable ships.","REVERSAL: The verified requirement says compliance must occur not later than 1 January of the year twenty years after the delivery year, so the prior no-earlier direction is not valid. Reverse the deadline comparison: require assessmentDate to be on or before 1 January of delivery-year-plus-20, using direct year/month/day logic without dynamic date construction. Preserve the ship target, applicability evidence, IA/IA Super alternatives, valid xsd:date operands, required delivery/assessment dates, and the two permitted method alternatives."],"current_feedback":"The conditional obligation is implemented as a presence-only method test: an applicable ship passes if it has any permitted method even when it also has invalid or multiple method values. Enforce exactly one ship-owned engineOutputComplianceMethod from the two permitted alternatives within the applicable branch, while retaining the required valid ship-owned deliveryDate and assessmentDate and the existing on-or-before 1 January of delivery-year-plus-20 comparison. Preserve the valid constructionStageDate applicability evidence, IA/IA Super alternatives, ship target, and xsd:date datatypes.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
